# LitricOS root dm-verity readiness
#
# cryptsetup first creates an empty device-mapper container, then changes it
# into the verified root mapping.  systemd's stock rule has already recorded
# the empty container as not ready, and the change event asks udev not to run
# unrelated rules.  Tell systemd about exactly the mapping that veritysetup
# just created.  The guards intentionally exclude all other dm devices.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="dm-[0-9]*", ENV{DM_NAME}=="root", ENV{DM_UUID}=="CRYPT-VERITY-*", ENV{SYSTEMD_READY}="1"
